<title>UK: London Tea Auction price indications.</title>
<headline>London Tea Auction price indications.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>At today's London landed Tea Auction of 6,018 packages of 53.50 kgs, including 1,600 offshore, price indications in pence a kilo compared to the last sale and the corresponding week last year.</p>
<p>    Best available  170     (137     and 260)</p>
<p>    Good		130     (128     and 160)</p>
<p>    Good Medium     123     (120     and 126)</p>
<p>    Medium	    114     (112     and  92)</p>
<p>    Low Medium	 90 nom ( 90 nom and  80)</p>
<p>The highest price paid was 170 pence for a Rwanda PF.1</p>
</text>
